{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-82179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-82179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{∘}\\le \\theta \\le {90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/assets/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the values on the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡({300}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nHowever, ${300}^{∘}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with ${300}^{∘}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract ${360}^{∘}.$\n\n$$\n{300}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=-{60}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-82179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0e41e674a2e310958f5a3889ed2f916ca1f6a46d3cd0a1bc1b29dfac5fef70f"} {"question" "q-82179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-82179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "-{60}^{∘}"] ["math" "-{90}^{∘}"] ["math" "{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "{45}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-82179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{60}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-90536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-90536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/assets/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the values in the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract $2\\pi .$\n\n$$\n\\frac{7\\pi }{4}-2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-90536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0e41e674a2e310958f5a3889ed2f916ca1f6a46d3cd0a1bc1b29dfac5fef70f"} {"question" "q-90536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-90536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-90536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{\\pi }{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-117412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$10\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-117412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/assets/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the values in the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract $2\\pi .$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1) & =10\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-5\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-117412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0e41e674a2e310958f5a3889ed2f916ca1f6a46d3cd0a1bc1b29dfac5fef70f"} {"question" "q-117412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-117412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5\\pi "] ["math" "-\\frac{10\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "10\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-117412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5\\pi "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-117456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-117456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{∘}<\\theta <{90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and fourth quadrants.\n\nSince $1$ is positive, our answer is an angle that lies in the first quadrant, where the tangent is positive.\n\nFrom the special values of the trigonometric functions, we know that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡({45}^{∘})=1.\n$$\n\nSince ${45}^{∘}$ is an angle in the first quadrant that lies within the range of $arctan,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)={45}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-117456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0e41e674a2e310958f5a3889ed2f916ca1f6a46d3cd0a1bc1b29dfac5fef70f"} {"question" "q-117456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-117456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0}^{∘}"] ["math" "{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "{45}^{∘}"] ["math" "{60}^{∘}"] ["math" "{90}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-117456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{45}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-320730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Expressed in degrees, $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=${{field-1}}${}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-320730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{∘}<\\theta <{90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and fourth quadrants.\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ is negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the fourth quadrant, where the tangent is negative.\n\nFrom the special values of the trigonometric functions and the oddness of the tangent function, we know that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-{30}^{∘})=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSince $-{30}^{∘}$ is an angle in the fourth quadrant that lies within the range of $arctan,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})={-30}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-320730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0e41e674a2e310958f5a3889ed2f916ca1f6a46d3cd0a1bc1b29dfac5fef70f"} {"question" "q-320730" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"} {"question" "q-320730" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-30"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/state.json" "file_sha256" "b205e5dc9e6d4d76c6fee799387419cd3fb214bf6a9c2c7df6afc66e40cbbe1f"}] "usage" {} "basis" 831 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
